## Proof

**Answer: 2033.**

**Setup.** Starting from $n=2022$, each step replaces $n$ by $n+d$ where $d\mid n$, $d>1$. Note $2022 = 2\cdot 3\cdot 337$.

**Step 1 — All even numbers $\ge 2022$ are reachable.**
$2022$ is even. If $n$ is even, then $2\mid n$, so $d=2$ is a legal move giving $n+2$ (still even). By induction, every even $n\ge 2022$ is reachable.

**Step 2 — Characterizing reachable odd numbers.**
An odd number can only be reached from an even number: if $n$ is odd, every divisor of $n$ is odd, so $n+d$ is even. Thus an odd $m$ is reachable iff there exist an even $n\ge 2022$ and an odd $d>1$ with $n+d=m$ and $d\mid n$.

Since $n=m-d$ and $d\mid n=m-d$ iff $d\mid m$, the condition becomes:

$$m \text{ (odd)} \text{ is reachable} \iff \exists\text{ odd } d>1:\ d\mid m \text{ and } d\le m-2022.$$

**Step 3 — All odd composites $\ge 2035$ are reachable.**
Let $m\ge 2035$ be an odd composite and $p$ its smallest prime factor. Then $p\ge 3$ is odd, $p\mid m$, and $p\le\sqrt m$. We need $p\le m-2022$.

- For $m\ge 2069$: $\sqrt m\le\sqrt{2069}<46\le 47\le m-2022$, so $p\le m-2022$. ✓
- For $2035\le m\le 2067$ (odd), check each odd composite individually using its smallest prime factor $p$ and the bound $p\le m-2022$:

| $m$ | factorization | $p$ | $m-2022$ | reachable? |
|-----|---------------|-----|----------|-----------|
| 2035 | $5\cdot 407$ | 5 | 13 | ✓ |
| 2037 | $3\cdot 679$ | 3 | 15 | ✓ |
| 2041 | $13\cdot 157$ | 13 | 19 | ✓ |
| 2043 | $9\cdot 227$ | 3 | 21 | ✓ |
| 2045 | $5\cdot 409$ | 5 | 23 | ✓ |
| 2047 | $23\cdot 89$ | 23 | 25 | ✓ |
| 2049 | $3\cdot 683$ | 3 | 27 | ✓ |
| 2051 | $7\cdot 293$ | 7 | 29 | ✓ |
| 2055 | $3\cdot 5\cdot 137$ | 3 | 33 | ✓ |
| 2057 | $11^2\cdot 17$ | 11 | 35 | ✓ |
| 2059 | $29\cdot 71$ | 29 | 37 | ✓ |
| 2061 | $9\cdot 229$ | 3 | 39 | ✓ |
| 2065 | $5\cdot 413$ | 5 | 43 | ✓ |
| 2067 | $3\cdot 13\cdot 53$ | 3 | 45 | ✓ |

(The remaining odd values 2027, 2029, 2039, 2053, 2063 in this range are prime, hence unreachable but not composite.)

**Step 4 — The odd composites 2023 and 2033 are unreachable.**

- $2023 = 7\cdot 17^2$. Odd divisors $>1$: $7,17,119,289,2023$. For each, $n=m-d<2022$ (e.g. $d=7\Rightarrow n=2016$). Unreachable.
- $2033 = 19\cdot 107$. Odd divisors $>1$: $19,107,2033$. For each, $n=m-d<2022$ ($d=19\Rightarrow n=2014$; $d=107\Rightarrow n=1926$; $d=2033\Rightarrow n=0$). Unreachable.

**Step 5 — Conclusion.**
Every even number $\ge 2022$ is reachable. Every odd composite $\ge 2035$ is reachable. The only unreachable odd composites are $2023$ and $2033$. Since $2033>2023$, the largest composite number of containers Marcus can never have is

$$\boxed{2033}.$$

